ret = DEFAULT_BUFSIZE;
```
Reason:
The original implementation only checks if the MTU is greater than or equal to 8KB to set the buffer size, which limits the maximum buffer size to 8KB. This causes issues when handling packets larger than 8KB, as the RX buffer size does not accommodate the maximum MTU of 16KB.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (mtu >= BUF_SIZE_8KiB)
```
```c
ret = BUF_SIZE_16KiB;
```
Reason:
The patch modifies the condition to check for MTU values greater than or equal to 8KB and sets the buffer size to 16KB accordingly. This change allows the RX buffer size to support larger packets, thus accommodating the maximum MTU of 16KB and resolving the issue.


